  "title": "The model lineup widened across text, image, audio, and video",
  "summary": "More models arrived, while the tools for finding them, sharing their output, and understanding their usage grew up around them.\n\nMuse Spark 1.1, GPT Realtime 2.1, Sana, GPT-OSS 20B, six additional text models, and HappyHorse 1.1 joined the lineup. Video gained distinct 720p and 1080p Veo 3.1 Fast options. Model descriptions and docs were updated to make capabilities and resolution choices easier to understand.\n\nNew community models now default to Private: owners can register and call them without listing them for everyone. Eligible publishers can make models Public, with visibility and pricing controls in the dashboard and Polli CLI. A daily Discord leaderboard and Model Monitor’s speed comparison offer more ways to see how community models perform.\n\nUploads gained optional tags and paginated public galleries, while untagged files remain unlisted. The upload limit rose to 100 MB, SDK uploads gained tag support, and uploads now receive unique URLs. CatGPT, AI Dungeon Master, and several community apps began publishing generated images to galleries or tagged media storage.\n\nEnter’s Activity tab brought API usage, app markup earnings, and community model rewards into a paginated events feed, with filters and charts for Pollen or request counts. Exports now distinguish API keys, and duplicate events no longer inflate reports. Two BYOP Quests added rewards for logging in through an app and for an external user logging in through an app owner’s authorization flow. Model listings also gained clearer Quest and Paid labels.",
